        {
          "id": 634637665,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": ">That will lead to clang at least removing that check away.\n\nYes, it's so clearly unnecessary that the compiler even removes it. So let's remove it from the source code :)\n\n> Null dereference for indirection is not undefined behaviour\n\nCalling `event->button()` on a null `event` is certainly UB.",
          "author": {
            "id": 620868,
            "username": "nicolas17",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Nicolás Alvarez",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/82fc14a8d756131416a2f108bbdd6009b2ba9df642adc22729ba38ca05c8cc00?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/nicolas17"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-24T19:27:23.896Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-24T19:27:23.896Z",
